{"id": "EUVD-2026-102274", "enisaUuid": "a190160c-7df9-3461-ab0c-7c953384d55c", "description": "Libyal libesedb through 20260704 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libesedb_record_get_multi_value() that allows attackers to read past buffers via unbounded multi-value offset tables. Attackers can supply a crafted ESE/EDB database processed by esedbexport to crash the application or expose up to about 32 KiB of adjacent heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:26", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libesedb-multi-value-offset-table-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libesedb/blob/cf49b6d420d4a44dcd6355bc0d6b36f9f580f350/libesedb/libesedb_record.c#L3776-L3830", "https://github.com/libyal/libesedb", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libyal-libesedb-through-20260704-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libesedb-record-get-multi-value"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gfhx-xwq8-3vw7", "CVE-2026-111147"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "109d7475-8dd9-3591-b05d-9092ae0ada11", "product": {"name": "libesedb", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260704"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "83274357-8e1e-3eee-953c-5eec798fa8fb", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}